{"content":[{"c":["RIGHT HAND"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["The word “right” in the Bible is often used in the sense of “being straight”; it is used to describe that which is just or righteous (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.18.25","r":"Gen.18.25","rawR":"Gen.18.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.18.25","value":"Gen.18.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 18:25"},"). Figuratively speaking, God’s right hand is the means whereby victories are obtained for the people of God (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.17.7,98","r":"Ps.17.7,98","rawR":"Ps.17.7,98","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.17.7,98","value":"Ps.17.7,98"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 17:7, 98:1"},"); it is also an instrument of punishment for the ungodly (",{"href":"?bref=Hab.2.16","r":"Hab.2.16","rawR":"Hab.2.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hab.2.16","value":"Hab.2.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hb 2:16"},"). While the right hand of man is impotent to save (",{"href":"?bref=Job.40.14","r":"Job.40.14","rawR":"Job.40.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.40.14","value":"Job.40.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 40:14"},"), God’s right hand sustains his children in the hour of need (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.139.10","r":"Ps.139.10","rawR":"Ps.139.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.139.10","value":"Ps.139.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 139:10"},"). Furthermore, God promises to strengthen the right hand of the person he purposes to help (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.41.13","r":"Isa.41.13","rawR":"Isa.41.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.41.13","value":"Isa.41.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 41:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["To be at the right hand of God is to occupy a place of the choicest blessings (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.16.11","r":"Ps.16.11","rawR":"Ps.16.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.16.11","value":"Ps.16.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 16:11"},"); it is the place where the Lord Jesus Christ now reigns in glory and intercedes for those he has redeemed (",{"href":"?bref=Rom.8.34","r":"Rom.8.34","rawR":"Rom.8.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.8.34","value":"Rom.8.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 8:34"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["To offer the right hand of fellowship is to extend the warmest and most accepting type of camaraderie (",{"href":"?bref=Gal.2.9","r":"Gal.2.9","rawR":"Gal.2.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gal.2.9","value":"Gal.2.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gal 2:9"},"). Giving the right hand as the sign of a pledge also has a biblical antecedent (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.10.15","r":"2Kgs.10.15","rawR":"2Kgs.10.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.10.15","value":"2Kgs.10.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 10:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Although the left hand is often linked to blessings (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.3.16","r":"Pr.3.16","rawR":"Pr.3.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.3.16","value":"Pr.3.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 3:16"},"), it may also be associated with treachery or other undesirable activity (",{"href":"?bref=Eccl.10.2","r":"Eccl.10.2","rawR":"Eccl.10.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eccl.10.2","value":"Eccl.10.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eccl 10:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Hand_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Hand_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Hand_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Hand"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"RightHand","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 18:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.18.25","rawQueryValue":"Gen.18.25","sourceRefExact":"Gen.18.25"},{"anchorText":"Pss 17:7, 98:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.17.7,98","rawQueryValue":"Ps.17.7,98","sourceRefExact":"Ps.17.7,98"},{"anchorText":"Hb 2:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Hab.2.16","rawQueryValue":"Hab.2.16","sourceRefExact":"Hab.2.16"},{"anchorText":"Jb 40:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.40.14","rawQueryValue":"Job.40.14","sourceRefExact":"Job.40.14"},{"anchorText":"Ps 139:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.139.10","rawQueryValue":"Ps.139.10","sourceRefExact":"Ps.139.10"},{"anchorText":"Is 41:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.41.13","rawQueryValue":"Isa.41.13","sourceRefExact":"Isa.41.13"},{"anchorText":"Ps 16:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.16.11","rawQueryValue":"Ps.16.11","sourceRefExact":"Ps.16.11"},{"anchorText":"Rom 8:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rom.8.34","rawQueryValue":"Rom.8.34","sourceRefExact":"Rom.8.34"},{"anchorText":"Gal 2:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gal.2.9","rawQueryValue":"Gal.2.9","sourceRefExact":"Gal.2.9"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 10:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.10.15","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.10.15","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.10.15"},{"anchorText":"Prv 3:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.3.16","rawQueryValue":"Pr.3.16","sourceRefExact":"Pr.3.16"},{"anchorText":"Eccl 10:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Eccl.10.2","rawQueryValue":"Eccl.10.2","sourceRefExact":"Eccl.10.2"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"48e0850e2d444e50bc8e74d0a7d1e7ed48110bac5d9873901fd48055747f17ef","sourceItemName":"RightHand","sourceItemOrder":150,"sourceMember":"Articles/R.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"RightHand","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Right Hand","title":"Right Hand","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}